SplitMind patch 0011 for OpenConnector v1.9.2 (after 0001-0005 and 0009).
Upstream issue: not filed yet.
Email watch pre-enable fixes: #104 outcome-only mail_watch runs, #105 redact codes in subjects, #106 standalone retention sweep, #107 drop List-Id.
From 6dfd3847552eb25eebe1e47064ca46d3b8a12eea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SplitMind <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:22:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(email-watch): pre-enable fixes for #104, #105, #106, #107

#104: every mail_watch run is recorded outcome-only by ActionRunner, whatever
the caller or audit value.
#105: runs of 4 or more digits (split by single spaces or hyphens) are
replaced with [redacted] in stored subjects and the dedup key.
#106: the retention sweep is a standalone function the cron calls on every due
minute, with or without a configured connection. It also deletes items and
cursors of connections that are no longer watched, and is a silent no-op when
the tables are missing. The once-a-day sweep is removed.
#107: List-Id is no longer requested; four metadata headers remain.
